window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Salvation comes not from perfection, but from the courage to face the truth, and the fire to rise from the ashes.</p> <p>In a realm scarred by generations of war and bitter feuds, hope is all but extinguished. The land’s last sanctuary has fallen, and five priests, each burdened by regret, shame, and longing, are forced into exile. They are not warriors. They are not kings. They are flawed men of faith, called to heal a world their ancestors helped divide.</p> <p>Haunted by the wounds of the past, these unlikely pilgrims must undertake a perilous journey: to climb the mountain and seek out the ancient dragons believed lost to legend. As they grapple with their own failures and confront the legacy of old sins, they begin to understand that reconciliation is born not of conquest, but of courage, truth, and forgiveness.</p> <p>In their hands lies the fragile hope of a fractured realm. To restore peace, they must bridge the divides that have torn their world, and themselves, apart.</p> <p>Dragon Riders of Old is an epic fantasy of faith, redemption, and the power of unlikely heroes. For listeners who yearn for stories where healing takes precedence over glory, and where the bravest act is to face the wounds no sword can mend.</p>"; 
